            {
                "entry_id": "25a02535-bcf3-3863-a3a6-bf693196ab38",
                "word": "devon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f4950307-07f8-449c-be91-574bd30d2742",
                        "entry_id": "25a02535-bcf3-3863-a3a6-bf693196ab38",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "devons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2a52ef7a-8461-3b53-a276-9fbc70eaa0cf",
                        "entry_id": "25a02535-bcf3-3863-a3a6-bf693196ab38",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Poisson artificiel servant d’appât."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3bbf7be-f3da-4d75-84a3-ba772eb06e8a",
                                "sense_id": "2a52ef7a-8461-3b53-a276-9fbc70eaa0cf",
                                "text": "Je lui ai montré comment plomber la ligne de façon que le devon — vous savez sans doute que c’est le nom donné au poisson artificiel — de façon que le devon, dis-je, ne navigue ni trop près du fond, ni trop près de la surface."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6976849-0cb7-4c15-b000-4501e845a5c1",
                                "sense_id": "2a52ef7a-8461-3b53-a276-9fbc70eaa0cf",
                                "text": "Lors de notre récente visite à la fin avril , les poissons aux multiples coloris réagissaient bien avec des petits tubes, des devons de moins de 11 cm et les traditionnelles cuillères métalliques accompagnées d’un ver de terre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92f63d29-9753-472c-b285-fb5df53dde5f",
                                "sense_id": "2a52ef7a-8461-3b53-a276-9fbc70eaa0cf",
                                "text": "Sur le fond, et autour de l’aquarium, des présentoirs exhibaient les attirails, des plus simples aux plus compliqués : gaules en bambou, cannes en fibre de verre, grandes cannes télescopiques pour moulinet à tambour tournant, boîtes de mouches et de cuillères, d’hameçons et de plombs, devons, moulinets de tous calibres, montures pour poissons morts, dégorgeoirs, bourriches, épuisettes, appâts réputés fantastiques ! fabuleux ! ou, plus prosaïquement, épatants !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c357b247-53c4-4bc5-a728-855520e5dae7",
                        "source_entry_id": "25a02535-bcf3-3863-a3a6-bf693196ab38",
                        "source_sense_id": "2a52ef7a-8461-3b53-a276-9fbc70eaa0cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "minnow",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "minnow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ede358f7-8423-3d83-bf08-6e144549bd88",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89bfaa4e-bb1d-45bb-9dd0-d5497f9fdf93",
                                                "sense_id": "ede358f7-8423-3d83-bf08-6e144549bd88",
                                                "text": "I have obſerved, as I have ſat by a ſpout of vvater, vvhich decſends from a ſtone trough about tvvo feet into a ſtream belovv, at particular ſeaſons of the year, a great number of little fiſh called minums, or pinks, throvv themſelves about tvventy times their ovvn length out of the vvater, expecting to get into the trough above."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7d74201-444d-4ec0-97d9-beb244913406",
                                                "sense_id": "ede358f7-8423-3d83-bf08-6e144549bd88",
                                                "text": "I wonder King George is let venture down on this coast, where he might be snapped up in a moment like a minnow by a her'n, so near as we be to the field of Boney's vagaries!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73a9d985-8cbf-4c69-a480-1989ffe4eee2",
                                                "sense_id": "ede358f7-8423-3d83-bf08-6e144549bd88",
                                                "text": "During the past week he had indulged in sundry sly purchases, […] They included […] a remarkable collection of fishing tackle, which the sporting-goods man had declared fitted to catch anything that swam, from a whale to a minnow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1afda8c7-d576-3896-8af2-3ebf6e60f3d2",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small fish.",
                                            "The common minnow (Phoxinus phoxinus), a small freshwater fish of the carp family Cyprinidae which has a green back with black elongated blotches, commonly swimming in large shoals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0a2e3fa-a981-4104-a952-4ccb7e39881a",
                                                "sense_id": "1afda8c7-d576-3896-8af2-3ebf6e60f3d2",
                                                "text": "Most minnows are small fish with cycloid scales, soft rays supporting their fins, and toothless jaws. Some possess barbels on their upper jaw, and many species develop nuptial tubercles during the breeding season. […] Minnows are arguably the most difficult group of freshwater fishes to identify, in part because they are often small and thus the characters distinguishing them are correspondingly small."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae9f775e-5e4d-398f-b1da-5d9bf44467eb",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small fish.",
                                            "Chiefly with a qualifying word: any of a number of other (small) fish from the family Cyprinidae; also (chiefly US), other small (usually freshwater) fish from other families."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81cb4751-3247-30d5-9632-d50850b2d8b4",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small fish.",
                                            "Synonym of galaxiid (“any member of the family Galaxiidae of mostly small freshwater fish of the Southern Hemisphere”); specifically, the common galaxias, inanga, or jollytail (Galaxias maculatus)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ff320f5-8de3-38c0-bdac-cb7a4449651b",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small fish.",
                                            "Synonym of stickleback (family Gasterosteidae)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "regional"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5272d72e-69b4-479e-8bc1-68eceeec889a",
                                                "sense_id": "1ff320f5-8de3-38c0-bdac-cb7a4449651b",
                                                "text": "In quiet, sheltered places, where the water is clear but does not run too swiftly, the ‘minnie,’ as the stickleback is locally called, makes its nest by the bank. […] On these fibres the ova are deposited, and they are then either purposely partly covered with sand by the minnie, or else the particles that are brought down by the current gather over the bundle of fibres and conceal it, excepting one small spot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or thing of relatively little consequence, importance, or value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bd6944b-1a44-4fce-9b74-1b15ed3401b3",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "Let him denie that there was another shewe made of the little minnow his Brother, Dodrans Dicke, at Peter-houſe, called, Duns furens. Dick Harvey in a frenſie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09927141-10fb-4226-9f00-afddc5dbc063",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "Heare you this Triton of the Minnoues?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b3cf3a0-331c-4515-9662-51ef3cd38b08",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "[H]e was in the receipt of some per centage on its dealings; and, participating in all its facilities for the employment of money to advantage, was considered, by the minnows among the tritons of the East, a rich man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce0e277f-5878-4810-b575-fe1238ba63b2",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "Having spent more than £500,000 on players last summer, Crawley can hardly be classed as minnows but they have still punched way above their weight and this kind of performance means no-one will relish pulling them out of the hat in Sunday's draw."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c1f3a90-6cdb-4f05-a700-b481d6574f6b",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "[…]Swed House signed contracts with Ikea's former production sites, swelling from being an online retailer into an operation employing 100 people and running 10 shops across Russia and Belarus[…] . But it remains a minnow compared with its Swedish predecessor, which employed 15,000 people and made $1.5bn in revenues during its last financial year in Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbdb2a35-06cd-4306-9765-1dfff0fbdd13",
                                                "sense_id": "51f80e8d-1b5b-3a8f-addc-028a781f5e06",
                                                "text": "The breadth of the potential impact became clear in an odd feature of the tariff list: Mr. Trump reserved his steepest rates not for America’s more economically advanced trading partners, but for economic minnows across Africa and Asia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b90d2c6-7144-3fa9-91e6-af611342819f",
                                        "entry_id": "cd257989-4221-38fb-9aae-7f05dabc7f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An artificial bait in the form of a small fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49d302a2-66f3-475a-84af-4799de7c74ee",
                                                "sense_id": "5b90d2c6-7144-3fa9-91e6-af611342819f",
                                                "text": "[…] I have (which I will show you) an artificial minnow, that will catch a trout as well as an artificial fly, and it was made by a handsome woman that had a fine hand, and a live minnow lying by her: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
